# Windows checkouts turn LF into CRLF, and several kinds of file here are read
# by Linux, where the stray \r is not whitespace:
#
#   *.sh   — the shebang becomes `/usr/bin/env bash\r` and the VPS answers
#            "bad interpreter: no such file or directory"
#   *.conf — nginx folds the \r into the token and rejects the directive
#   .env*  — `POSTGRES_PASSWORD=secret\r` makes the \r part of the password,
#            which then does not match the one in DATABASE_URL
#
# So these stay LF wherever they are checked out.
*.sh          text eol=lf
*.conf        text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf
*.sql         text eol=lf
.env          text eol=lf
.env.*        text eol=lf
*.example     text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
